@preamble let system = import("system")
args
Returns the arguments supplied to the Aiki program, excluding the interpreter
name and source filename. REPL and embedded sessions have no program arguments
unless the host supplies them.

args()

type(system.args())    # :list
===
env
Returns the value of the named host environment variable as a string. If the
variable is not set, returns [@error, :environment, msg].

env(name)

is_error(system.env("AIKI_VARIABLE_THAT_IS_NOT_SET"))    # true
===
cwd
Returns the working directory owned by the current Aiki runtime. The runtime
working directory controls relative filesystem operations and process
execution without mutating the embedding Go process's working directory.

cwd()

type(system.cwd())    # :string
===
chdir
@unchecked
Changes the working directory of the current Aiki runtime. path must identify
an existing directory. Returns true on success or [@error, :io, msg]. This does
not change the embedding host process's working directory.

chdir(path)
===
exec
@unchecked
Runs command synchronously with the supplied list of string arguments. The
child process uses the current Aiki runtime working directory.

A process that starts successfully returns [@ok, stdout, stderr, exit_code],
even when exit_code is nonzero. Failure to start the process returns
[@error, :process, msg].

exec(command, args)
